# Changelog (engine/v1/)

## CONFIG values are raw numbers

**What:** Every spatial value in `API_CONFIG` (`ENGINE.Config`) is now a plain number with its unit named in a comment: `Debug.Levels.BoundingBox.Grid.Size` (CNU), `Physics.Gravity.Strength` (CNU/s²), `Physics.Gravity.TerminalVelocity.Air/Water` (CNU/s), `Physics.Buoyancy.Force.Min/Max` (CNU/s²), `Physics.Buoyancy.GradientDepth` (CNU), `Camera.ZoomStep` (CNU). `Camera.Fov` and `Physics.Correction.MaxAngleDelta` are labelled degrees. Engine reads drop `.value`; the debug grid converts with `CNUtoWorldUnit`. Forces.js drag coefficients are now functions that read CONFIG live, not import-time constants. The engine-only exports in config.js stay Unit-instanced. UNIT_INSTANCING.md gained a §1 "Exception: CONFIG".

**Where:** [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [Forces.js](engine/v1/math/Forces.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Camera mode angles are Units

**What:** orbitCam's `yaw`/`pitch` and freeCam's persisted view `yaw`/`pitch` are degree Units; chaseCam/sideCam's `side`/`settle` are radian Units. A reusable `chaseRuntime.look` holds the chase frame's look as degree Units. `consumeLookInput` writes `.value` on the view's Unit yaw and pitch, and readers convert with `.toRadians()`/`.toDegrees()`.

**Where:** [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js)

## Camera and movement angles passed between functions are Units

**What:** In camera modes, `settlePitch`, `armPitch`, `chasePitch`, `gapToTrail` and `stiffen` return radian Units. `pitchWindow` takes a Unit settle and returns degree-Unit `top`/`bottom`/`min`/`max`. `chaseFreedom` returns those plus a radian-Unit `yaw`; its `minPitch`/`maxPitch` fields became `min`/`max`. `consumeLookInput` takes Unit pitch bounds, and `armAt`/`armBasis` take Unit angles. `wrapDegrees` wraps a degree Unit in place, and a read-only `noTurn` zero-radian Unit was added. `modeData.yaw` from freeCam and orbitCam is a radian Unit. The player input frame's `previousCameraYaw` and `lockAngle` are radian Units; `advanceCarriedForward` and `lockedDirection` take Unit angles. `cameraState.fov` was removed: the projection matrix and loop framing read `CONFIG.Camera.Fov` directly.

**Where:** [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Spatial rates are instanced

**What:** Character meta `maxSpeed` (CNU/s), `acceleration`/`deceleration` (CNU/s²) and `momentumTurnRate` are now Units, instanced next to `jumpHeight`. `momentumTurnRate` is authored in degrees/s (14 rad/s → 802.14 on all four characters) and converted with `.toRadians(true)`. `level.player.metaOverrides` instances the same keys plus `jumpHeight`, now taken as a plain number instead of `{ value }`. The default model turn rate is `new Unit(458.37, "degrees").toRadians(true)`, cloned into each entity's `modelTurnRate`; the player scales it into radian Units. `turnFacingToward` and `stepModelRotation` take a Unit max step. `CONFIG.Physics.Correction.ReferenceReleaseRate` is 229.18 degrees/s (was 4 rad/s), converted where it's used. The camera loop tracker's `turned`/`arcTurn` (radians) and `arc`/`radius` (CNU) are Units. `PlayerHeight` returns a CNU Unit, and `sceneGraph.loopSurfaces` radii are CNU Units. Already-instanced velocities and speeds are labelled per second where they're instanced. UNIT_INSTANCING.md gained a §1 "Rates" subsection.

**Where:** [characters.json](engine/v1/player/characters.json), [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [Model.js](engine/v1/player/Model.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Unit and UnitVector3 are engine-exclusive

**What:** `ENGINE.Math.Instancing` (`Unit`, `UnitVector3`) was removed from the game API, along with the now-unused import in ini.js. MODULE_GROUPS §3 and UNIT_INSTANCING §1 now state that `Unit`/`UnitVector3` are engine-exclusive: games never receive them, and math/ never uses them.

**Where:** [ini.js](engine/v1/core/ini.js), [MODULE_GROUPS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/MODULE_GROUPS.md), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Game-exposed force math takes a plain water level

**What:** `ComputeBuoyancy`, `ComputeSubmergence` and `ComputeStepVelocity`'s buoyancy input take `waterLevel` as a plain CNU number or null instead of a Unit. physics/Forces.js unwraps the scene's water-level Unit through a new `waterLevelOf`, which passes null through. Movement's buoyancy step-sim passes `waterLevel: 0`.

**Where:** [math/Forces.js](engine/v1/math/Forces.js), [physics/Forces.js](engine/v1/physics/Forces.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js)

## Shared CloneTransform and Unit.math

**What:** `Unit.math(f, ...args)` sets the value to `f(value, ...args)` and returns the Unit. It is used for the camera's obstruction distance smoothing and the player's jump apex tracking. `CloneTransform` (math/Utilities.js, exposed as `ENGINE.Math.Other.CloneTransform`) copies a transform. Instanced position, rotation and pivot are cloned as UnitVector3, plain ones are copied as plain vectors, scale is always copied, and pivot is copied only if present. It replaces NewEntity.js `cloneRootTransform`/`cloneLocalTransform`, and the inline copies in Matrix.js `CreateRenderMatrixCache` and Animation.js `buildModelPose`/`applyPartLocal`. `applyModelPose` builds `model.posedTransform` directly with it. Scale is now copied where it used to be shared with the source. UNIT_INSTANCING.md gained a §3 exception for `CloneTransform`'s `instanceof` check and a §7 `.math` pattern.

**Where:** [Utilities.js](engine/v1/math/Utilities.js), [Matrix.js](engine/v1/math/Matrix.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [ini.js](engine/v1/core/ini.js), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Capsule colliders reach full height again

**What:** `CapsuleFromAabb` clones `segmentEnd` from the box center before `segmentStart` shifts down, so the segment spans the full box height instead of ending at the center.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js)

## Animated decals on flat faces are no longer cut to their rest footprint

**What:** `flatDecalFacets` grows the flat decal quad (positions and UVs) by the decal's animation margin, the same margin curved hosts already use. `decalAnimationMargin` also accounts for spin, adding √2 when any keyframe rotates the decal.

**Where:** [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Overlap push uses the shallower of collider and box depth

**What:** `DetectCurrentPhysicsOverlaps` measures how far the entity's AABB and the candidate's AABB overlap along the contact normal. It pushes the entity out by whichever is smaller: that box overlap or the collider's contact depth. The candidate AABB is looked up once and reused for both the overlap gate and the depth.

**Where:** [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js)

## Grounded model turns at the full rate

**What:** Entities have a `modelTurnRate.ground` rate, the default 450°/s with no scaling; the player reuses the base entity's. `resolveModelPose` uses the water rate when underwater, the ground rate when grounded, and the air rate otherwise.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)

## Player model turns at the full rate out of water

**What:** The player's `modelTurnRate.air` (out of water) is the base rate with no `airControl` scaling. `water` still scales by `underwaterAirControl`. The `modelTurnRate.ground` key from the previous entry is removed again, and `resolveModelPose` uses water when underwater and air otherwise.

**Where:** [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)

## Dead face-remapping code removed from entity parts

**What:** Removed `remapRotatedFaces`, the `faceMap` part field and its writes in `buildModel`, and the unused `builtPosition`/`builtRotation`/`builtScale` part fields. `builtDimensions` stays. The `BestMatchOf` import is dropped.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)

## Entity bounds scaling and rest-pose save use shared helpers

**What:** `computeScaledBounds` scales sphere, capsule and compound-sphere radii (and the capsule half-height) with `scaleUnit`. `captureRestCollision` saves the root transform with one `CloneTransform` call.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)

## Loop-surface detection split out of surface chunking

**What:** Loop-surface detection moved from `buildSurfaceChunks` into a new `findLoopSurfaces(pieces, owner, facets, links)`, which also computes the per-facet incline. `buildSurfaceChunks` builds pieces, links and chunks, then calls it. Its `{ chunks, loopSurfaces }` return is unchanged.

**Where:** [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js)

## Chase camera's post-loop return works again

**What:** `PrepareCamera` reads `cameraState.looping` into `wasLooping` before the situation updates, and sets `frame.leftLoop = wasLooping && !cameraState.looping`. `leftLoop` is true again on the frame a loop situation ends, so `prepareChase` starts its return.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js)

## "last" prefix for state from before

**What:** Names holding earlier state now use `last`:
- `loop.lastUp`/`lastPosition`, `frame.lastMode` (was `from`) and `lastLooping` in the camera.
- orbitCam's `lastDirection`, and chase's `lastPitch`/`pitch` (was `pitch`/`nextPitch`).
- The entity input frame's `lastCameraYaw`/`lastHasInput`/`lastGrounded`/`lastUp`/`lastKeys`/`lastControl`.
- `physicsRuntime.lastPosition`/`lastRotation`, and physics' `lastGrounded`.
- `playerState.lastAction`.
- `hasMeaningfulVectorDelta(vector, corrected)`.
- `MeasureRefreshRate`'s `lastTime`.

The player action event's `from`/`to` keys are unchanged. ENGINE_SEMANTICS gained §6 "Last and Next". The old §6 is now §7.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [Performance.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Performance.js), [ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md)

## Past-tense booleans and the action event's keys

**What:** Booleans that hold whether something was true now use the past tense:
- `wasLooping` in `PrepareCamera` and `wasGrounded` in physics, replacing `lastLooping`/`lastGrounded`.
- The entity input frame's `wasGrounded` and `hadInput`, replacing `lastGrounded`/`lastHasInput`.

The `PLAYER_ACTION_CHANGE` payload's `from`/`to` keys are now `lastAction`/`action`, and `SetPlayerAction` takes `action`.

ENGINE_SEMANTICS §6 now covers the was/had form for booleans and limits `next` to deliberate use: the next item in a sequence, or a value calculated ahead.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md)

## Sprite part shape (0.35.5)

**What:**
- New `"sprite"` shape for entity parts and particle parts: a camera-facing quad. On terrain or obstacle parts it is dropped with a warning.
- Options come from the new `spriteOptions` schema: `distanceScaling`, `follow` (`full` | `horizontal`), `range`, `occludedRange` and `image` (`{ path, sourceType }`).
- Sprite bounds are a cube of half-side `hypot(x, y)/2`, so they enclose every facing.
- `SpriteProgram` faces the quad in the vertex shader. It holds a constant screen size when `distanceScaling` is false, using a 10 CNU reference, and fades on distance over the last 15% of `range`/`occludedRange`.
- Sprites always draw in the sorted translucent pass. `drawSortedRuns` groups by program (uv/triplanar/sprite).
- `drawSpriteThroughWalls` runs after the translucents with `depthFunc(GREATER)` for sprites within `occludedRange`. `hideOccluded` skips entities flagged `showsThroughWalls`.
- Sprite images load in normalize and Instance, and register as `sprite::<path>` textures.

**Where:** [NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js), [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewTemplate.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTemplate.js), [NewTexture.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTexture.js), [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js)

## Mipmaps on static scene textures

**What:** Every non-animated scene texture gets `generateMipmap` and `LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR`. Animated textures stay `LINEAR`.

**Where:** [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`ensureSceneTexture`)

## Particle shape override

**What:**
- Particle requests and authored particles accept a `shape` override. All six override schema copies list it; capsule, tube and ramp-complex are excluded.
- A sprite override without sprite options gets the defaults.
- The entity geometry cache key now includes the part shape.

**Where:** [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json)

## Content-keyed decal textures

**What:**
- Decal texture keys are now `decal::customTexture::` + the decal's content signature (including its `mutable` flag) + its face size. They are computed once at build as `ct.textureKey`.
- Entities and particle groups that share part ids no longer overwrite each other's decals. Scatter decals use the same key.

**Where:** [NewTexture.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTexture.js), [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js)

## Particle spawns no longer throw

**What:** `synthesizeGroupDefinition` reads `resolved.physics` in place of an undefined `mode`.

**Where:** [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js)

## Level blueprint image decals receive their bitmaps

**What:** After image loads finish, `shareBlueprintBitmaps` points each merged entity's image decals, decal sources and sprite images at its blueprint's loaded bitmaps. Failed loads are then filtered on the merged parts too.

**Where:** [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js)

## Sprites don't collide

**What:**
- `computeEntityAabb` leaves sprite parts out of the entity box, unless every part is a sprite.
- Entities carry a build-time `spriteOnly` flag. A sprite-only entity that isn't a particle gets no collision candidates, is skipped as a broadphase candidate for others, and is skipped in the combat hurtbox loop.
- Sprite particles keep their particle physics mode.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Performance.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Performance.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js)

## Sprite tuning in config

**What:** `SPRITE_TUNING` in config.js (outside `API_CONFIG`) holds `FadeStart` (0.85) and `ScreenSizeDistance` (10 CNU). `SpriteProgram` reads both instead of inline values.

**Where:** [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js)

## Sprites become plane options; crossed planes; entity visual bounds (0.35.5 rework)

**What:**
- `"sprite"` is no longer a shape. Planes take `primitiveOptions { crossed, sprite }` (new `planeOptions` schema). `sprite` is null or `{ follow, distanceScaling, range, occludedRange, image }`, and `follow` now accepts `none | horizontal | vertical | full`.
- Every plane is an upright x-by-y quad facing +Z. Normalize zeroes a plane's `dimensions.z`. Crossed planes are two quads at ±45° around the height.
- Sprite and crossed planes work on entity parts, terrain, obstacles and obstacle parts. They default to `aabb` collision, and their decals are dropped with a warning. Scatter grass parts use `crossed: true`, the automatic scatter twin is gone, and the low tier lost its 90° tilt and ×10 scale.
- Every mesh carries `mesh.sprite` (sprite options or null), which drives shader choice, translucency, the through-walls pass and occlusion exemption for terrain, obstacles and entities. A following sprite's bounds are a cube of half-size `hypot(x, y)/2`.
- `SpriteProgram` builds per-mode axes (follow codes 0–3) from the model's own right/up/front.
- Entities carry `visualBounds`, the box around every part, and the distance cull, frustum and occlusion culling, Simulator framing and particle centering read it. `entity.collision` is null when no part adds to bounds; such an entity's buoyancy, resistance, correction and collision stages are switched off at build, and combat and collectibles skip it. `spriteOnly` and `entityRenderBounds` are removed. `collision.shape` and `collision.detailedBounds` are removed in favour of `collision.physics.shape`/`.bounds`.
- The particle `shape` override is removed from `overrideKeys` and all six schema copies.
- `computeWorldAabb` + `boxCorners` replace `ComputeWorldAabbFromBounds`; `UpdateObjectWorldAabb(mesh, rough)` takes the rough-box choice.
- `drawSpriteThroughWalls` filters the sorted translucent list. Terrain texture size reads x and y for planes. The water top is built as a plane rotated −90° on x. `InscribedBox` treats z as a plane's flat axis and gives crossed and sprite planes no blocker.
- Comment cleanup across the touched modules.

**Where:** [NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js), [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewTexture.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTexture.js), [NewTemplate.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTemplate.js), [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [textures.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/textures.json), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Performance.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Performance.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js), [Collectible.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Collectible.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [player/Model.js](engine/v1/player/Model.js)

## Entity full box and collision box

**What:**
- `entity.visualBounds` is renamed `entity.fullAabb` (the box around every part), and `model.restBounds` is renamed `model.restFullAabb`.
- `GetSubmergence` reads `fullAabb` instead of `collision.aabb`. Buoyancy and resistance therefore work on entities without a collision box.
- For entities with no colliding parts, `BuildEntity` turns off only correction and collision. It warns only when correction was authored on.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [physics/Forces.js](engine/v1/physics/Forces.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [Performance.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Performance.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js), [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js)

## Sprite follow side limit; sprites write depth

**What:**
- Horizontal and vertical sprite follow turn toward the camera only until the front is 90° from the authored front. Past that they hold at the side limit (GLSL `limitFacing` in `SpriteProgram`). Horizontal measures from the model's front projected flat. Vertical tilts around the model's right, limited by the model's front.
- Sprite runs in the translucent pass write depth (`drawSortedRuns`), so crossed sprite halves hide each other.

**Where:** [Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Sprite follow aligns to the camera's view

**What:**
- Horizontal and vertical sprite follow now align to the camera's viewing direction (`cameraBack`, from the view matrix) rather than the direction to the camera's position. This replaces the side-limit `limitFacing`, which is removed.
  - Horizontal faces `cameraBack` flattened to the ground.
  - Vertical faces `cameraBack` minus its component along the part's right.
- The `u_cameraPosition` sprite uniform and its upload are removed.

**Where:** [Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Vertical sprite hinge follows the screen

**What:** Vertical follow reverses its hinge (the part's right) whenever it points against the camera's right. `cameraRight` is now computed once alongside `cameraBack`.

**Where:** [Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js)

## Launch off a surface releases it

**What:** In `GetSurfaceCorrection`, a ground hit while the entity is `launched` and its velocity points away from that surface's normal now returns `releasedSurface`.

**Where:** [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js)

## Carried forward argument order restored

**What:** `advanceCarriedForward` again carries the heading across (`carryAcross`), rotates it by the camera yaw delta, then projects it onto `up`.

**Where:** [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js)

## Camera aims at the shown model

**What:** `AimPoint` aims at the collision box center as the shown model holds it: the body position, plus the pose anchor turned by the body rotation, plus the scaled rest box center minus the anchor, turned by the shown rotation. A new `shownRotation` helper (the model pose rotation, or the transform rotation with animations disabled) is shared with `modelFlip`. Modes.js now imports `PoseAnchor` from physics/Correction.js.

**Where:** [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js)

## Particle generators attach to a carrier face

**What:**
- **Generator fields.** Every generator `particle` block, and `particleRequest`, gains `side` (a face; expected, fallback `top`) and `area` (a spawn box). `position` now offsets from that face's center, in carrier axes.
- **Placement.** `GeneratorPlacement` returns a generator's offset, world position and carrier rotation. Groups spawn at a random point in the area and launch with velocity turned by the carrier. `follow()` refreshes the rotation, and re-turns the offset only when the carrier turned. Bursts keep world axes and have no area. Center emission is gone.
- **Exports and targets.** `GetFaceCenterOffset` is exported (renamed from `getFaceCenterOffset`). `findSceneTarget` also returns the target mesh, through the new `targetMesh`.

**Where:** [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewTemplate.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTemplate.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js)

## Scatter quality tiers removed

**What:**
- **Quality setting.** `Performance.Scatter.Quality` is `"High"` or `"Low"`. Low draws every scatter part that isn't already a crossed plane as a crossed plane, keeping its x/y size and decals.
- **Engine scatter data.** Scatter parts no longer split fields by tier, and their `primitive` field is renamed `shape`. `resolveTier` and `instanceTiers` are gone.
- **Engine JSON keys.** Scatter parts carry `primitiveOptions`, leaves and branches carry `complexity`, and the halfpipe's `shared` carries `destructible`/`hp`/`static`.

**Where:** [textures.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/textures.json), [terrain.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/terrain.json), [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Game-authored templates

**What:**
- **Payload field.** Level payloads take an optional `templates` object with `textures`, `scatter`, `particles`, `terrain`, `obstacles`, `npcs`, `projectiles` and `playerCharacters`, each keyed by id.
- **New schema roots.** `textureTemplate`, `scatterTemplate`, `scatterTemplatePart`, `particleTemplate`, `objectTemplate`, `objectTemplateShared`, `partRepeat`, `entityTemplate`, `playerCharacterTemplate`.
- **Validation.** `validateTemplates` runs first in `ValidateLevelPayload`.
- **Normalization.** `normalizeGameTemplates` runs first in `LevelPayload`, in dependency order, into the same shape Instance.js produces. The result is stored on `normalized.templates` and `ctx.templates`.
- **Lookups.** `findTemplate` resolves every template lookup game-first, then engine. The load-time `templateIds` sets are removed.
- **Registration.** `RegisterGameTemplates` / `ClearGameTemplates` write game templates into the instanced engine collections and restore any engine entries they replaced. `npcs` fill both characters and enemies. `BuildLevel` registers and `ClearLevel` clears.
- **Simulator.** `Simulator.Start` caches engine entries after clearing the active level.
- **Fixes in the same files.**
  - `normalizeAttacks` returns its normalized entries.
  - Validation shares a `validatePartList` helper.
  - An object template part with `color` but no texture tints a copy of the shared texture.

**Where:** [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [validate.js](engine/v1/core/validate.js), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js)

## CreateLevel clears a running level first

**What:** `CreateLevel` calls `ClearLevel(false)` before validating whenever a level is running, and keeps the "end levels naturally" warning. The later stop of a still-active loop is removed.

**Where:** [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js)

## Shared particleGenerator schema

**What:** A new `particleGenerator` root holds the generator fields (`id`, `side`, `area`, `position`, `overrides`). The `particle` field of `levelPart`, `levelObject`, `templateObjectRef` (root and `parts[]`) and `templateEntityRef` `model.parts[]` is now a plain object field that refers to it. `normalizeGenerator` fills authored generators from that root before `normalizeParticle`, which no longer accepts null.

**Where:** [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js)

## Engine player decals load at boot

**What:** `loadTemplateDecalBitmaps` also loads the image decals of `player/characters.json`, resolving their paths from `player/`, and `loadBitmap` takes the folder paths start from. Model.js no longer loads or filters decals: `loadDecalBitmaps`, `filterDeadDecals` and its `NormalizeImage` import are removed. `BuildPlayerModel` is no longer async, and `hasCustomParts` is no longer passed to it.

**Where:** [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [Model.js](engine/v1/player/Model.js), [Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js)

## Scatter models spin as a whole

**What:** Each scatter model draws one random spin (`modelYaw`) instead of one per part. Part offsets turn around the model origin with it, in the placement loop and in the root-part footprint checks (`rootPartFootprintAabbXZ` now takes `modelYaw`).

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## Low-quality scatter decals and skipLow

**What:**
- **Flat parts.** At Low quality, a flat part (thinnest along y) becomes one horizontal sheet. Its `top` decals move to the sheet's front, with their position turned to match.
- **Other parts.** Every other part becomes a crossed pair that keeps only its front and back decals.
- **`skipLow`.** A new scatter type flag; when true, the type is skipped entirely at Low. Leaves and branches set it, and `scatterTemplate` accepts it.

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [textures.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/textures.json), [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json)

## Low-quality flat part test narrowed

**What:** At Low quality, a scatter part only counts as flat when its height is at most a tenth of the smaller of its width and depth. The flat sheet sits where the part's top face was. This replaces the "thinnest along y" test from the entry above.

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## Scatter root parts must stand on the parent

**What:** `areRootPartsWithinParentBounds` now also rejects a model when any corner of a root part's footprint lies outside the parent's detailed bounds. The check is the new `isFootprintOnParent`, using the part yaw plus the model yaw.

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## math/Geometry.js split out of math/Collision.js

**What:**
- **New `math/Geometry.js`.** Exports `TriangleNormal`, `TriangleArea`, `TriangleCentroid`, `TriangleAabb`, `MeshTriangles`, `AabbCenter`, `AabbHalfExtents`, `PointsAabb`, `BoxCorners`, `SphereFromAabb`, `CapsuleFromAabb`, `ObbFromAabb`, `OffsetDetailedBounds`, `SplitPolygonByPlane`, `ClosestPointOnSegment` (was private `closestPointOnSegment`) and `ClosestPointOnTriangle`.
  - `MeshTriangles(positions, indices, matrix)` is new. It places each corner once and shares it between triangles. It replaces the loops in NewObject's `computeTriangleSoupFromMesh` and NewVoid's `buildWorldTriangles`.
  - `BoxCorners(box)` is new. It returns the 8 corners with x changing fastest, then y, then z. It replaces NewObject's `boxCorners` and the corner lists in NewEntity's `placeAabbEnclosure` and NewTerrain's `occluderPiece`.
- **`math/Collision.js` exports** are now `AabbOverlap`, `AabbOutsideFrustum`, `TriangleDistanceSq`, `PointInsideMesh`, `BuildTriangleGrid`, `TriangleGridCandidates`, `PointInsideTriangleGrid`, `MeshesIntersect`, `SweptAABB`, `RayAABBIntersect`, `RayAABBDetailedBoundsIntersect`, `RayTriangleIntersect`, `SegmentQueryBox`, `TriangleInQueryBox`, `RayDetailedBoundsIntersect`, `SweptSphereBounds` and `NarrowphaseContact`. `raySphereIntersect`, `rayOBBIntersect`, `rayCapsuleIntersect` and `rayTriangleSoupIntersect` are now private.
- **Velocity math.** `ApplyDeceleration` is now `ComputeDeceleration` in `math/Forces.js`. `ClampVelocity` and `ProjectOntoPlane` moved to `math/Vector3.js`. `ApplyAcceleration` is now private `applyAcceleration` in `player/Movement.js`.
- **Moved into their only consumer as private functions:**
  - `physics/Collision.js`: `expandAabbY`, `horizontalApproach`, `slideAlongContacts`, `pointAabbFaceGap`, `pointObbFaceGap`, `reachesTriangle`, `nearestFrontTriangle`.
  - `physics/Correction.js`: `surfaceAlignedRotation`.
  - `builder/NewTerrain.js`: `inscribedBox`, `voidCutBoxes`, `subtractBox`, `aabbLargestFace`, `mergeTouching`, `solidBoxes`.
  - `handlers/Render.js`: `projectBoxCorners`, `convexHull2D`, `cornersInsideHull`, `beyondFrontFaces`.

**Where:** [Geometry.js](engine/v1/math/Geometry.js), [Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js), [Forces.js](engine/v1/math/Forces.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [physics/Forces.js](engine/v1/physics/Forces.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js), [NewTerrain.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTerrain.js), [NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js)

## Terrain blocker inscribed box no longer NaN

**What:** `inscribedBox` scales the dimensions by `0.5` instead of by `ToVector3(0.5)`, which made every component NaN. Terrain blockers get through the size filter again.

**Where:** [NewTerrain.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTerrain.js)

## Scatter parent outline checks fixed

**What:** `isPointInDetailedBoundsXZ` destructures `center` for its OBB branch. `fitsParent` multiplies the part's dimensions by the `localScale` vector before scaling by the uniform scale.

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## Box folds go through PointsAabb

**What:**
- **NewObject.** New private `readVertices` (vertex objects from a flat x, y, z list) and `unitBox` (a plain box as UnitVector3 corners). `generateSphereUvs`, `computeBounds` and `computeWorldAabb` fold through `PointsAabb`.
- **`MergeAabb(boxes)`** now takes a list of boxes instead of `(accumulator, box)`. `BuildObstacle` and the Simulator's two calls pass mapped lists.
- **`processScatterModels`** merges every part's box with `PointsAabb`. The checks for a missing box or an empty model are gone.
- **`occluderPiece`** builds its world box with `PointsAabb`.

**Where:** [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [NewTerrain.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTerrain.js)

## Level build sub-processes: blockers, terrain chunks, loops

**What:**
- New directory `builder/subProcesses/`.
- **Occlusion.js.** Takes the terrain blocker code from NewTerrain. `BuildOccluders(terrain, voidTerrain)` replaces `CarveOccluders` and the blocker pass in `BuildTerrain`, building each mesh's blockers once with its voids cut out. Log: "Terrain blockers built: meshes=, carved=".
- **Chunks.js.** `AssembleTerrainChunks(terrain, voidTerrain)` replaces `buildSurfaceChunks`. It covers terrain and terrain-void linings only, and returns `{ chunks, pieces, owner, facets, links }`. `boxFacets` and `boundsFacets` moved with it. Log: "Terrain chunks: Chunks, Links, Ms".
- **Loops.js.** `FindLoops(terrainChunks, meshes)` returns `{ loopSurfaces, tubeCenterlines }` from the chunk links. Obstacles are no longer loop surfaces, and `tubeCenterlines` holds terrain and void-terrain centerlines only. Log: "Loop surfaces: Air, Water, Tubes, Ms".
- **math/Utilities.js.** New exports `MakeRoots`, `FindRoot`, `JoinRoots`.
- **NewLevel.** Calls `BuildOccluders`, `AssembleTerrainChunks` and `FindLoops` after `BuildVoidWalls`. `sceneGraph.chunks` is the chunk list.
- **NewTerrain.** Builds terrain only.
- **Level.js.** `SpawnIntoScene` calls `BuildOccluders(terrain, [])` for spawned terrain.

**Where:** [Occlusion.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Occlusion.js), [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js), [Loops.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Loops.js), [Utilities.js](engine/v1/math/Utilities.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [NewTerrain.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTerrain.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js)

## IsPointInSuppressingVoid renamed to IsCutByVoid

**What:**
- `physics/Collision.js` export `IsPointInSuppressingVoid` is now `IsCutByVoid`. Callers in physics/Collision.js, camera/Master.js and Chunks.js updated.
- Chunks.js: `boundsFacets` inlined into the terrain loop of `AssembleTerrainChunks`.

**Where:** [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js)

## destructible, hp and static are obstacle-only

**What:**
- **canonSchemas.json.** `destructible`, `hp` and `static` removed from `levelObject` and `objectTemplateShared`. New schema `obstacleFields` holds the three.
- **normalize.js.** `normalizeLevelObject(rawObject, ctx, role)` replaces the `multipartFallbackShape` parameter. Obstacles get `obstacleFields` merged on, and the multi-part `"triangle-soup"` collision fallback keys off `role === "obstacle"`. `normalizeObjectTemplate(rawTemplate, ctx, collection)` merges `obstacleFields` onto `shared` for the `obstacles` collection.
- **NewTemplate.js.** `ResolveObjectSource` copies the three fields only for role `"obstacle"`.
- **Engine JSON.** The three keys removed from the halfpipe's `shared` in terrain.json and the sim-disc terrain object in levels.json.

**Where:** [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [NewTemplate.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTemplate.js), [terrain.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/terrain.json), [levels.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/levels.json)

## normalize warns on unrecognized fields

**What:**
- **`normalizePayloadSchema`** warns "`<path>.<field>`: not recognized, dropped." for every payload field its schema doesn't list, at every nested layer, with full paths (array entries get `[index]`).
- **`normalizePayloadSchema(payload, rootKey, extraKey = null)`** merges a second schema's fields. Obstacles use it for `levelObject` + `obstacleFields` and `objectTemplateShared` + `obstacleFields`, replacing the two-call `Object.assign` merge.
- **`SimulatorPayload`** takes `payloadType` out of the payload before normalizing.

**Where:** [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js)

## Scatter High quality no longer draws planes

**What:** The Low-quality conversion check in `BuildScatterVisualResources`' part setup is `Quality !== "Low"`. It read `!Quality === "Low"`, which was never true. `sampleDimensions` is `part.dimensions.clone().scale(uniformScale)`.

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## Template and override resolution shortened

**What:**
- **`ResolveEntitySource`.** `platform`, `attacks`, `hardcoded`, `animations` and `customEvents` are cloned in one spread `structuredClone`. `hp` and `collisionOverride` use `??`. The root transform takes each field from the ref, or from the template where the ref is null, then goes through `CloneTransform`.
- **`ResolveObjectSource`** and **`ResolveTextureBlueprint`** use `??` for override-or-template fields.
- **`resolveCollisionOverride`.** `hurtbox` and `hitbox` are `source.x === null ? null : collisionOverride.x ?? defaults.x`.
- **`mergeTemplateRefEntity`.** `spawnSurfaceId` uses `??`. `dialogue` is destructured.

**Where:** [NewTemplate.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTemplate.js), [NewTexture.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTexture.js), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js)

## Obstacle, terrain and void mesh builders shortened

**What:**
- **NewObstacle.** The single-part path passes `...source` with its own `position` and `texture`. The multi-part path destructures the root fields like `buildTerrainParts`. The `scatterContext` blocks and the `index` parameter are removed. `BuildObstacle(source, options)` replaces `BuildObstacle(source, index, options)`.
- **NewTerrain.** `buildSingleTerrain` raises the terrain once, through `raisePartPosition`.
- **NewVoid.** `buildVoidMesh` builds one mesh; each texture branch sets only `geometry` and `material` (`{ ...defaultMesh.material }`, plus `textureScale: 1` on the tiled branch).

**Where:** [NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js), [NewTerrain.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTerrain.js), [NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js)

## Index grouping moved to Geometry.js

**What:** `MakeRoots`, `FindRoot` and `JoinRoots` moved from math/Utilities.js to a new LINKED GROUPS section in math/Geometry.js. Chunks.js and Loops.js import them from Geometry.js.

**Where:** [Geometry.js](engine/v1/math/Geometry.js), [Utilities.js](engine/v1/math/Utilities.js), [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js), [Loops.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Loops.js)

## CloneTransform moved to Vector3.js

**What:** `CloneTransform` moved from math/Utilities.js to math/Vector3.js, next to `CloneVector3`. Vector3.js imports `UnitVector3` from Utilities.js for its `instanceof` check. NewEntity, NewScatter, NewTemplate, ini.js, Animation, Simulator and Matrix.js import it from Vector3.js. NewScatter's unused `CloneVector3` import is removed.

**Where:** [Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js), [Utilities.js](engine/v1/math/Utilities.js), [Matrix.js](engine/v1/math/Matrix.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [NewTemplate.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTemplate.js), [ini.js](engine/v1/core/ini.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js)

## Chunk bounds, grid inside test and scatter opening boxes fixed

**What:**
- **`AssembleTerrainChunks`.** Void-lining pieces store their box as `worldAabb`, like terrain pieces, and the bounds reach reads `piece.worldAabb`.
- **`PointInsideTriangleGrid`.** The ray's grid entry is `(min − pad − point) / ray` again.
- **`iterateScatterInstances`.** The open-face box corners are named `faceMin`/`faceMax`.

**Where:** [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## Frustum test picks the box corner per axis

**What:** `AabbOutsideFrustum` picks each axis of the tested box corner from the sign of that axis of the view wall's normal, as plain arithmetic. It no longer makes one `CompareVector3` choice for all three axes.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js)

## Jump release gravity and slope jump damping

**What:**
- **Jump release.** `UpdateMovement` sets `playerState.gravityScale` to `MOVEMENT_TUNING.ReleaseGravity` while `action === "Jumping"`, `velocity.y > 0` and `input.jump` is not held. Coasting a loop lock still sets `modeData.coastGravityScale` first.
- **Slope jump.** At launch, the positive world-y part of the tangent velocity is scaled by `UphillJumpKeep + (1 - UphillJumpKeep) * max(up.y, 0)`. Downhill and sideways speed are unchanged.
- **Config.** `MOVEMENT_TUNING` gains `ReleaseGravity: 3` and `UphillJumpKeep: 0.25`.

**Where:** [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Entity `underwater` replaced by `medium`

**What:** The entity boolean `underwater` is replaced by `medium: "Air" | "Water"`. NewEntity defaults it to `"Air"`; the physics pipeline sets it from `submergence >= 0.5`. `ClassifySurface` takes `medium` in place of `underwater`. Correction.js's `angleLimitsFor` helper is removed; `MaxAngleDelta` and `MinGripSpeed` are indexed by `entity.medium` directly. `solveJumpLaunchVelocity` takes `"Water"`/`"Air"`. All readers updated.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Forces.js](engine/v1/physics/Forces.js), [Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)

## Loop engage/release events

**What:** camera/Master.js sends `PLAYER_LOOP_ENGAGED` `{ id, type, position, velocity, axis, center, radius }` and `PLAYER_LOOP_RELEASED` `{ id, type, position, velocity, reason }` through a new `sendLoopEvent`, gated by `playerState.customEvents.loop` and `CONFIG.CustomEvents.Entities.Loop` (new API_CONFIG key, default `false`). The "Loop engaged"/"Loop released" `Log` calls are removed. `releaseLoop(playerState, reason)` sends the release event and calls a new `resetLoop()`; `InitializeCameraState` calls `resetLoop()` directly. The player `customEvents` schema gains a `loop` flag.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json)

## Jump release ramp, slope damping reverted, no coast friction in the air

**What:**
- **Jump release.** The gate is `playerState.launched && action !== "Stunned"` (was `action === "Jumping"`), still with `velocity.y > 0` and jump not held. `gravityScale` ramps from `max(gravityScale, 1)` toward `ReleaseGravity` over `ReleaseRampMs` instead of switching instantly.
- **Slope jump.** The uphill damping at launch is removed; launch is `tVel + up * launchSpeed` again.
- **Air coasting.** New `coastFriction` (`friction` when grounded, `0` otherwise) replaces `friction` at both coast-deceleration sites (no-input branch and post-lock branch). `friction` and `staticFriction` are unchanged.
- **Config.** `MOVEMENT_TUNING.ReleaseGravity` 3 → 2; new `ReleaseRampMs: 200`; `UphillJumpKeep` removed.

**Where:** [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Jump release gravity ramps back down

**What:** When a jump is no longer released-and-rising, `gravityScale` steps back toward 1 by the same `rampStep` (`max(1, gravityScale - rampStep)`) instead of snapping to 1. Grounded sets `gravityScale` to exactly 1; coasting a lock still sets `coastGravityScale` first. The `ReleaseRampMs` comment covers both directions.

**Where:** [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Turning entities skip the per-part vertex fit (0.35.8)

**What:**
- `applyModelPose(model, fitBoxes)` always composes part transforms, and refits part world boxes (`UpdateObjectWorldAabb`) only when `fitBoxes` is true. The build-time calls in `buildModel` and `captureRestBounds` pass `true`.
- New entity field `fitsParts`, set once in `BuildEntity`. It is true when the physics, hurtbox or hitbox layer is `compound-sphere`. `refreshEntityDerivedState` passes it, so a rotation change refits part boxes only for those entities.
- `buildDebugBoundingBoxes` refits the part boxes of entities without `fitsParts` when debug boxes refresh. NewLevel.js imports `UpdateObjectWorldAabb` from NewObject.js.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js)

## Collision soups carry a triangle grid (0.35.8)

**What:**
- New `SoupBounds(type, triangles)` builds `{ type, triangles, grid }`, with the grid from `BuildTriangleGrid`. Triangle-soup bounds of meshes and multi-part obstacles and both void-lining soups are built with it.
- `deepestContactInBox` takes the soup. It, `aabbTriangleSetContact`, `rayTriangleSoupIntersect` (all indices for an infinite ray), `nearestFrontTriangle` and the fast-move trace in `DetectPhysicsCollisions` loop `TriangleGridCandidates`, keeping their `TriangleInQueryBox` filters.
- `TriangleGridCandidates` returns a single cell's list directly, or a shared empty list for an empty cell.
- Void entries carry `solidGrid` instead of `solidTriangles`: terrain voids reuse the carve grid, obstacle voids build one over all parts. `isVoidCancelled` and `IsCutByVoid` use `PointInsideTriangleGrid`. `PointInsideMesh` was removed. Occlusion.js reads `solidGrid.triangles`.
- A void lining's `floorBounds` or `wallBounds` is `null` when that side has no triangles. The broadphase, `probeVoidWalls` and `AssembleTerrainChunks` skip null sides.
- `CARVE_GRID_TRIANGLES_PER_CELL` also sizes the collision grids (comment only).

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js), [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js), [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js), [Occlusion.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Occlusion.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Variadic MinVector3 and MaxVector3 (0.35.8)

**What:**
- `MinVector3` and `MaxVector3` take any number of vectors.
- Chained calls were flattened in `TriangleInQueryBox`, `TriangleAabb` and `behindBlocker`. NewScatter's open-face box uses `TriangleAabb(face)`.
- `generateSphereUvs` passes `ToVector3(0.0001)` instead of a plain number, which gave a NaN radius.

**Where:** [Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [Geometry.js](engine/v1/math/Geometry.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js), [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js)

## Chunk-first collision broadphase (0.35.8)

**What:**
- New `AssembleCollisionChunks` in Chunks.js runs after `FindLoops`. Obstacles join the terrain chunks they touch by the facet-touch rule, and an obstacle touching two chunks merges them. Each chunk is `{ id, worldAabb, members }`. A member is `{ ref, type, rank, seq, aabb, linings }`, with void linings listed under their host, and the member box covers the host and its linings.
- `fitMember` and `fitChunk` fit the boxes. `AddChunk` gives a spawned terrain mesh or obstacle its own chunk. `RemoveChunkMember` removes it, refits only the chunk box and drops an empty chunk. `boundsFacets` and `expand` moved to module scope.
- `sceneGraph.chunks` holds the collision chunks (the old `{ id, surfaceIds }` list was replaced), and `sceneGraph.collisionSeq` holds the next order number for spawns.
- `BroadphaseCollectCandidates` walks chunks, then members, then linings, and sorts by `rank`/`seq` to keep the old candidate order. Triggers and entities are appended after the sort.
- `SpawnIntoScene` and `DespawnFromScene` keep chunks current. The Simulator rechunks an obstacle after moving it onto the platform.

**Where:** [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js)

## Debug bounds draws skip when every type is off (0.35.8)

**What:** `drawBoundingBoxes` and `drawDetailedBounds` return before binding the debug line pass and walking their records when every type of their kind is off. The record lists stay built.

**Where:** [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Entities rest (0.35.8)

**What:**
- An entity, the player included, is marked `physicsRuntime.resting` when a step leaves its position and rotation unchanged and its velocity still. `ApplyPhysicsPipeline` returns at once while it stays resting: velocity still, transform untouched, and no awake entity's box overlapping it (`touchedByMover`).
- Every entity reuses its overlap and ground results within a step until it moves (was player-only).
- `shouldSkipCollisionPipeline` and `physicsRuntime.cachePrimed` were removed.
- `wakeEntities` clears rest on every entity after any non-entity spawn and any despawn.

**Where:** [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js)

## 0.35.8 names and comments

**What:**
- Renames: `PointInsideTriangleGrid` → `PointInsideGrid`, `deepestContactInBox` → `deepestInBox`, `CARVE_GRID_TRIANGLES_PER_CELL` → `GRID_CELL_TRIANGLES`, `updatePhysicsRuntimeCache` → `recordStep`.
- `AssembleCollisionChunks` returns `{ chunks, seq }` (was `nextSeq`).
- Comments rewritten as plain one-liners in math/Collision.js, Chunks.js, physics/Master.js, physics/Collision.js and NewEntity.js. No behaviour change.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Chunks.js](engine/v1/builder/subProcesses/Chunks.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)

## Grid cell constant inlined (0.35.8)

**What:** `GRID_CELL_TRIANGLES` (formerly `CARVE_GRID_TRIANGLES_PER_CELL`) removed from config.js and its export. `BuildTriangleGrid` sizes cells with the literal `2` inline. math/Collision.js no longer imports config.js. No behaviour change.

**Where:** [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js)

## Scatter decals keep their rotation

**What:** `cloneScatterDecal` copies the decal's `localTransform` field by field: `position` and `rotation` through `.clone()`, `scale` through `CloneVector3`. The decal's `Unit` rotation is no longer turned into an `{x, y, z}` of `undefined`, so scatter batch decals get finite placement matrices. NewScatter imports `CloneVector3` in place of `CloneTransform`.

**Where:** [NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js)

## World size is `dimensions`, water height is `topY` (0.35.9)

**What:**
- **Payload.** `world.length`/`width`/`height` are replaced by `world.dimensions` (`vector3`, each axis ranged 1–100000), with x = old length, y = old height, z = old width. `world.water.level` is renamed `world.water.topY`.
- **Runtime.** normalize instances `world.dimensions` as a cnu `UnitVector3` and `world.water.topY` as a cnu `Unit`, clamped between `deathBarrierY` and `dimensions.y`.
- **Readers.** Trigger height and the water meshes (NewLevel), the default level camera's target and far plane (camera/Master), the physics water input (physics/Master), the water clip (Render) and the payload summary log (Level) read the new fields.
- **Authored data.** The simulator level, testGame's `levels.json` (both stages), `lvl2.json`, the stage 2 preprocessor and the LSM level use the new fields.

**Where:** [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js), [templates/levels.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/levels.json)

## Carl's brows are solid tubes

**What:** `browLeft` and `browRight` set `primitiveOptions.solid: true`, so they have no inner walls. Carl's base mesh drops from 7,756 to 6,692 triangles.

**Where:** [player/characters.json](engine/v1/player/characters.json)
